---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { docs, href } from '../config'
---
<Base title="CAD software alternatives for 3D modeling" description="Explore Prism, an alpha desktop CAD app for solid, surface and freeform modeling, simulation and manufacturing, when evaluating CAD alternatives.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width: 820px">
      <p class="kicker">Choosing CAD software</p>
      <h1>Exploring alternatives for 3D CAD?</h1>
      <p>Prism is a desktop CAD application for Windows, macOS and Linux. It combines sketch-driven solid modeling, surfaces and NURBS, freeform modeling, simulation, manufacturing tools and Python scripting in one workspace.</p>
      <h2>Evaluating a CAD alternative</h2>
      <p>If you are researching a Creo alternative, an NX alternative, a Fusion 360 alternative, or other 3D modeling tools such as Solid Craft, Prism may be worth evaluating for exploratory work. These products differ in capabilities, maturity, workflows and file compatibility; Prism does not claim feature parity or affiliation with them.</p>
      <h2>What to try in Prism</h2>
      <p>Start with a constrained sketch and build a solid, try a freeform shape or surface, then explore the simulation and manufacturing workspaces. Prism is in alpha and is not yet ready for production work. Review the <a href={docs('/reference/known-issues')}>known issues</a> and keep backups.</p>
      <p><a href={href('/features')}>Explore features</a> · <a href={docs('/guide/getting-started')}>Read the getting-started guide</a> · <a href={href('/download')}>Download Prism</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
